{"format":1,"seq":325,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The ToolContext type is still needed for readContextView, so I'll keep it. Now I'm adding constants for collapsed line byte limits and title/outcome character caps alongside the existing callNote logic in edits.ts.\n\nI'm defining a CollapsedCall interface for finished calls, plus helper functions that clip text to a character limit and safely truncate strings to a byte budget without splitting UTF-8 sequences, appending an ellipsis when cut. I should double-check the byte-cutting loop doesn't slice through a surrogate pair boundary.\n\nThen I'm writing a describeCall function that assembles the display line for a collapsed call—joining the tool name (for multi-call cases), a clipped title in quotes, the function list, and a clipped outcome string with a separator.\n\nStill writing helper logic...\n\nStill writing collapse logic...\n\nI'm validating that keepRuns and minTokens are proper integers within valid bounds, throwing errors otherwise, then returning the resolved settings. I'm also defining which message roles count as \"input\" for grouping into runs.\n\nNow I'm writing a function that groups context items into runs based on where input-role messages begin, iterating backwards from before the current run's first item. I need to handle the edge case where leading items appear before the first input message, like a summary header followed by kept assistant messages.\n\nThen I'm defining a helper to extract tool result messages, and a function to describe tool calls for display—starting with special handling for typescript calls by digesting their arguments and result into a collapsed summary.\n\nI'm writing a generic outcome helper: no result means \"no result\", errors show the first line of the error text, otherwise \"ok\". I'm thinking about whether to reuse logic from digestTypeScriptCall or just write a small local helper in collapse.ts that pulls the first line of text for the outcome.\n\nNow I'm sketching planCollapse: it checks if freeing tokens below a minimum threshold is even worthwhile, finds finished runs before the first kept run, and iterates through older items collecting collapsible results, pulling out tool calls from the assistant message and tallying tokens to free.\n\nChecking that the item's tool calls still have all original, unprotected results before treating them as collapsible.\n\nI'm also confirming that token counts for kept items properly include thinking blocks, and that edited assistant entries with \"stop\" reasons line up with the plain text message approach. Now I'm moving to the apply.ts changes, defining the task input shape with pending indices and collapse options.\n\nFor the apply phase itself, I'm building logic that fetches the conversation handle, commits a transaction gathering staged entries, flattens their edits and operations, and then—if collapse settings are provided—builds a context view from the active entries, runs a collapse plan starting from the given index, and pushes any resulting edits and provenance. Finally, if there's a handle and edits exist, it submits with the operations and pending data. I'm now noticing the view used for planning includes the currently pending staged entries from this same run, which could cause a conflict I need to resolve.\n\nI need to double-check type compatibility between the task runtime's transaction type and the tool execution API's transaction type, plus verify the conversationId type lines up correctly. For the hook factory, I'm defining a function that creates a hook registration taking optional collapse settings, where the after-run logic scans for pending entries and bails early if there's nothing pending and no collapse requested, otherwise building an input object with pending entries and optional collapse settings using the run's starting index. I'm debating whether to keep a default export for the no-collapse case since it's mainly useful for tests, and planning to add a test case covering a hook that requests a task with collapse settings even when nothing is staged—plus thinking about an optimization for when collapse is requested but no earlier runs actually exist.\n\nI realize I can add a cheap check for whether any entries exist before the run's starting point, and skip the task entirely if there are none, which avoids wasted work on first runs. I also need to confirm the run's starting index type is stored as a plain number, verify the input JSON conforms to the expected value type, and work out how collapse options flow through index.ts into the guidelines section and hook creation, plus how the collapse guideline text and related types propagate through the sections and session files. Now I'm ready to write out these files.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_018kv3SfQXihJpKLr2ukmN2A","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Get anchors in durable edits.ts imports and elisionStub\"}\nasync ({ workspace: { read } }) => read(\"src/durable/context/edits.ts\", { ranges: [[1, 16], [84, 90]] } as any)"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":5318,"cacheRead":115200,"cacheWrite":1563,"totalTokens":122083,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":5185},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794904743718,"responseId":"msg_bdrk_nnwk4a6sn7kny5huvb5plih3sqc3t5zjp337sebwfg5ebcepyh5a","rawStopReason":"tool_use","durationMs":47044,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}],"kind":"pi.assistant","id":94,"conversationId":1,"byTaskId":92}},{"type":"task","value":{"id":92,"conversationId":1,"kind":"pi.generation","version":2,"input":{},"background":false,"abortRequested":false,"state":{"status":"waiting","checkpoint":{"phase":"tools","assistant":94,"tools":[95],"pending"